 en:{plain:'In one sentence',symbols:'Every symbol explained',unit:'Unit',definition:'Meaning and recorded setting',example:'Work through an example',meaning:'How to read higher and lower',notation:'Read the notation first',notationText:'Subscripts are labels: ref means reference, in means inlet, eff means effective. Bold U is a vector with direction; |U| is its magnitude. Superscript 2 means squared; ⊤ transposes matrix rows and columns.',notationRows:[['≤','less than or equal to'],['max','take the larger value'],['ln','natural logarithm, used for the inlet-height profile'],['Σ','sum over mesh faces or samples'],['∫','sum small contributions over a continuous surface'],['∇ / ∇·','spatial change / net outflow per volume'],['Δ / |…|','retrofit minus baseline / absolute value or vector magnitude'],['U·n','boundary-normal velocity: outflow positive, inflow negative'],['√ / ·','square root / vector dot product, the sum of component-wise products'],['∇T / ∇·U','temperature change per metre (K/m) / net outflow per volume (s⁻¹)']],units:'Read the units',unitsText:'m means metres; m/s means metres per second. W is power: 1 W = 1 joule per second. W/m² is power per area. K is absolute temperature; a 1 K difference equals 1°C. 0.05 = 5%. kWh is accumulated energy, not interchangeable with W. kg is mass in kilograms, J is energy in joules, Pa is pressure in pascals; m² is area and m³ is volume. Unit 1 is dimensionless and can be shown as a percentage. W here describes heat power; building electricity is calculated separately.',readTitle:'Read the maps and numbers',walkTitle:'From inputs to a decision in eight steps',walkNote:'Each step has inputs, an action and an output. Read the workflow and indicators first; open equations as needed.',walkHeaders:['Input','Action','Output'],status:'What this page currently shows',checksTitle:'Check the calculation before interpreting the design'},
